# cpp-style.md §7.1 — layer 1. The only thing that actually enforces §3 naming.
---
Checks: >
  readability-identifier-naming,
  cppcoreguidelines-macro-usage,
  bugprone-*, performance-*, modernize-*,
  -modernize-use-trailing-return-type,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters

# The two exclusions above are decisions, not concessions (architecture-design.md §15.5h).
# They landed on 2026-08-11, the first run where clang-tidy 19 actually graded this repo.
#
# -modernize-use-trailing-return-type: this project writes LEADING return types. The style base is
#   Google (.clang-format) and every declaration in the tree follows it, so the check demanded 209
#   rewrites of a convention the project chose on purpose. It only ever appeared here via the
#   `modernize-*` wildcard.
# -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters: the surface where an argument swap is actually dangerous -
#   protocol, persistence, IDs - is already covered by the strong-typed IDs of cpp-style.md §4.3.
#   What is left is internal constructors, and wrapping those in structs is a redesign, not a fix.

# Diagnose headers under atlas/ ...
HeaderFilterRegex: '[/\\]atlas[/\\]'
# ... but never generated output (cpp-style.md §7.1: generated code is excluded).
ExcludeHeaderFilterRegex: '[/\\]generated[/\\]'

CheckOptions:
  - { key: readability-identifier-naming.ClassCase,             value: CamelCase }
  - { key: readability-identifier-naming.FunctionCase,          value: CamelCase }
  - { key: readability-identifier-naming.TypeAliasCase,         value: CamelCase }
  - { key: readability-identifier-naming.VariableCase,          value: lower_case }
  - { key: readability-identifier-naming.PrivateMemberSuffix,   value: _ }
  - { key: readability-identifier-naming.NamespaceCase,         value: lower_case }
  - { key: readability-identifier-naming.MacroDefinitionCase,   value: UPPER_CASE }
  - { key: readability-identifier-naming.MacroDefinitionPrefix, value: ATLAS_ }
  - { key: readability-identifier-naming.GlobalConstantPrefix,  value: k }
  # cpp-style.md §3 says `constexpr` is kPascalCase REGARDLESS of scope, and without this pair
  # the rule only held at namespace scope. readability-identifier-naming resolves an identifier at
  # the most specific level that has ANY option set: a namespace-scope `constexpr` stopped at
  # GlobalConstant (prefix above, so `kMaxPayload` passed), but a function-local one found nothing
  # set until it fell all the way through to VariableCase — and was told to be lower_case. The
  # convention was inverted for locals, which is why `kSentinel` and `kPosterThreads` were errors.
  - { key: readability-identifier-naming.ConstexprVariableCase,   value: CamelCase }
  - { key: readability-identifier-naming.ConstexprVariablePrefix, value: k }
  # Encodes cpp-style.md §5 instead of switching the check off: the ATLAS_ family (log · throw ·
  # check) is the sanctioned macro set, and everything outside it stays a violation.
  - { key: cppcoreguidelines-macro-usage.AllowedRegexp,         value: '^ATLAS_' }
